  "full_text": "So, Mr. God, what do you think of my Texas relatives? You know, it's very obvious that the virtue of the cowboy was rewarded with oil. That's, in my mind, it seems really obvious. So, the virtue of the cowboy was rewarded with oil. So, God says something. For thus saith the Lord, Behold, I will make thee a terror to thyself and to all thy friends, and they shall fall by the sword of their enemies. And then I shall behold it, and I will give all Judah into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall carry them captive to Babylon, and shall slay them with the sword. I'll make thee a terror to them. I scare myself sometimes. A lot. Good. Expected. So God said, If I read this book out loud, I get emasculated. I hate when it happens. See, because what goes around comes around. And if you become a real scary person, a monster, then there are consequences. The little monster gets a little scared.",
